Even worse is that if the player has warning or TP they can step back 
and forth and get the monsters to split off one at a time to be dealt with.

There ought to be just a few "tight mazes" on very special levels.

One of the levels that could use the current Gehennom style layout would 
be a special level between Medusa and the Castle where the one and only 
Minotaur resides.

This level would be unteleportable (even by liches) and unmappable with 
undiggable walls and floors and the only thing that starts there is the 
only Minotaur in the game.

The Minotaur would have the current physical attributes, but untamable 
with a high level of magic resistance plus half a dozen random 
resistances.  He knows the maze by heart and so is not only immune to 
traps, but he also uses the maze solver to track down heroes by scent.

So instead of simply pointing out the upstair as currently, all warning 
would do is tell you the shortest path between where the Minotaur is now 
and your current location.

